1
00:01:49,159 --> 00:01:50,840
Hey, you still up?

2
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,840
There's an update on Dai Mingming's case.

3
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,079
What did they say?

4
00:01:56,079 --> 00:01:57,959
The Political and Legal Affairs Commission coordinated today.

5
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,239
Dai Yumei was granted release on bail.

6
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,239
Release on bail.

7
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,480
That's a pretty good result.

8
00:02:06,959 --> 00:02:07,560
Don't you think

9
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:11,639
the result is good,

10
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,919
but the root of the problem isn't solved?

11
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,879
Dai Yumei's health won't hold up for much longer.

12
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:20,759
And Dai Mingming isn't adapting to the welfare home.

13
00:02:24,319 --> 00:02:24,800
I mean,

14
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,080
I just don't know how

15
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,360
this will turn out in the future.

16
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:30,159
But...

17
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,520
at least we have a buffer period now, right?

18
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,199
If any other problems arise,

19
00:02:34,439 --> 00:02:36,560
we'll figure them out together.

20
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,479
I'm just anxious.

21
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,560
How can I truly help her?

22
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,360
Can you help me?

23
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:44,840
Will you?

24
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:46,280
I need help too.

25
00:02:47,159 --> 00:02:47,759
What's wrong?

26
00:02:47,919 --> 00:02:49,560
It's Liao Bufan.

27
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:50,919
He has such a weird temper.

28
00:02:51,639 --> 00:02:52,960
We barely exchange two words before...

29
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,439
his... his anger just flares up.

30
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:55,360
It just keeps rising.

31
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:56,840
It makes the work

32
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:57,919
really hard to carry out.

33
00:02:59,479 --> 00:03:00,319
Is he...

34
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,439
like this with everyone,

35
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,479
or is he just targeting you?

36
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,080
It's not just me.

37
00:03:08,919 --> 00:03:09,520
Guys like him...

38
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:12,919
He isn't married, right?

39
00:03:13,599 --> 00:03:14,680
How did you guess?

40
00:03:17,199 --> 00:03:19,159
Once you have a family, that temper disappears.

41
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,280
Never mind. Get some rest.

42
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,159
Wait, wait, wait.

43
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:31,080
Don't hang up yet.

44
00:03:31,159 --> 00:03:33,680
I still have something to... to discuss with you.

45
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:36,000
Go ahead.

46
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,599
It's about our... our thing.

47
00:03:39,599 --> 00:03:41,319
You... you brought it up last time.

48
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:47,479
I've been analyzing and thinking about it lately.

49
00:03:49,039 --> 00:03:50,599
Really, thinking about it seriously.

50
00:03:51,199 --> 00:03:52,280
Here's what I think.

51
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,520
Hear me out and see if this works.

52
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,840
Our relationship...

53
00:04:02,039 --> 00:04:03,400
Could we... could we maybe...

54
00:04:04,159 --> 00:04:06,879
just cool off for two or three months first?

55
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:22,319
You... If you don't say anything, I'll take it as a yes.

56
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:23,399
Good night.

57
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:24,360
Sweet dreams.

58
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:05,720
Old Wei.

59
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,360
Well, here's the thing.

60
00:05:07,759 --> 00:05:08,879
First thing tomorrow morning,

61
00:05:09,279 --> 00:05:11,480
I'll drop by the courtyard to see you. We need to talk.

62
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:12,680
Alright.

63
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,240
Okay, okay, okay.

64
00:05:28,759 --> 00:05:30,439
Chief Guo, we have to handle this.

65
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,879
The child was really scared by the gunshots.

66
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,360
The child also has congenital dilated cardiomyopathy.

67
00:05:37,519 --> 00:05:38,600
I consulted Dr. Chen.

68
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:41,480
She said this condition needs immediate treatment.

69
00:05:48,839 --> 00:05:49,720
Our SWAT detachment

70
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,920
is worried sick right now.

71
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:52,839
All because of this child.

72
00:05:54,759 --> 00:05:55,439
It seems

73
00:05:56,839 --> 00:05:58,040
you're starting to fit in.

74
00:06:00,079 --> 00:06:00,600
That's good.

75
00:06:02,639 --> 00:06:04,560
It's thanks to your timely guidance.

76
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:05,519
All right.

77
00:06:05,839 --> 00:06:06,519
It's true.

78
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,319
You quickly helped me find

79
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,839
the right approach to my work.

80
00:06:10,439 --> 00:06:12,519
A political officer isn't just icing on the cake,

81
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,040
but a lifeline in times of need.

82
00:06:14,759 --> 00:06:15,639
Whatever the team needs,

83
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:16,800
I'm here to resolve it,

84
00:06:17,319 --> 00:06:18,959
and shoulder my responsibilities as a commissar.

85
00:06:33,959 --> 00:06:34,279
Alright.

86
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,319
Stay around at noon.

87
00:06:36,639 --> 00:06:37,439
Let's have lunch together.

88
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,240
I'll pass. Maybe next time.

89
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,560
I'm going to find Dr. Chen.

90
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:41,360
Thanks, Chief.

91
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,079
Chief Guo.

92
00:06:50,519 --> 00:06:52,720
The issue with our SWAT detachment's training ground

93
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:53,920
still hasn't been resolved.

94
00:06:54,519 --> 00:06:55,519
The skills competition is coming up soon.

95
00:06:56,439 --> 00:06:58,000
When can it be fixed?

96
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,639
You never leave empty-handed, kid.

97
00:07:00,639 --> 00:07:01,519
Let's talk while we eat.

98
00:07:02,439 --> 00:07:04,199
Respected leaders and comrades,

99
00:07:04,319 --> 00:07:06,720
today, filled with guilt and remorse,

100
00:07:06,879 --> 00:07:08,199
I am writing this self-criticism letter

101
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:11,160
to express my deep realization regarding

102
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,920
my bad habit of taking arbitrary leaves.

103
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:14,120
Over the past year,

104
00:07:14,439 --> 00:07:16,079
my total leave time has exceeded...

105
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,920
Did you eat lunch?

106
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:30,639
I did.

107
00:07:32,839 --> 00:07:34,399
Then read it louder.

108
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,319
Report!

109
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,439
The preserved pork at the cafeteria today was a bit salty.

110
00:07:39,879 --> 00:07:40,680
It made my throat sore.

111
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:46,920
Too salty, huh?

112
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,160
Old Liu.

113
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,160
Go to the equipment room and get the megaphone.

114
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,160
Take the team to the main gate.

115
00:07:52,199 --> 00:07:53,160
Have him read it at the gate.

116
00:07:54,199 --> 00:07:54,560
Yes, sir.

117
00:07:58,199 --> 00:08:00,000
Report! My throat is better now.

118
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:01,800
If you dare slack off again,

119
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,480
I'll put you in a patrol car

120
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,959
and make you read it all over Hongye.

121
00:08:05,399 --> 00:08:05,959
Yes, sir.

122
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,079
Commissar Tan.

123
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,120
Commissar Tan.

124
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:16,879
Is Dr. Chen in?

125
00:08:16,879 --> 00:08:18,160
She went to the restroom.

126
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:19,600
I'll wait for her.

127
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,040
Okay.

128
00:08:43,519 --> 00:08:44,879
I didn't expect my moving out

129
00:08:44,879 --> 00:08:46,960
to traumatize you so much.

130
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,399
I'll move back in tomorrow.

131
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,080
It has nothing to do with you.

132
00:08:58,519 --> 00:08:59,600
I was already coming here before that.

133
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,519
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

134
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,120
Would it have helped if I told you?

135
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,720
Ideological work is my specialty.

136
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,320
I could've analyzed it perfectly for you.

137
00:09:13,879 --> 00:09:14,600
Come on, tell me.

138
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,240
This isn't ideological work.

139
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,000
It's psychological counseling.

140
00:09:22,559 --> 00:09:23,759
I know about that.

141
00:09:24,879 --> 00:09:26,120
There are plenty of methods.

142
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,919
But you have to tell me your situation first.

143
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:30,480
Right?

144
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,639
I'll... I'll think of something for you right now.

145
00:09:34,519 --> 00:09:35,360
Treat me as your sounding board.

146
00:09:35,639 --> 00:09:36,279
Pretend you don't know me.

147
00:09:37,559 --> 00:09:38,519
Open up your heart.

148
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,039
Pour out all the bottled-up

149
00:09:42,159 --> 00:09:42,840
bitterness in your heart,

150
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,679
those hidden

151
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,320
frustrations,

152
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,039
and those lingering

153
00:09:51,919 --> 00:09:52,600
doubts.

154
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,159
Pour them all out to me.

155
00:09:54,799 --> 00:09:56,720
I'm the best at finding the problem.

156
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:01,440
Or... you name a method.

157
00:10:03,639 --> 00:10:04,720
I want you to be quiet.

158
00:10:07,279 --> 00:10:07,720
Quiet.

159
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:14,840
You're awake.

160
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,279
What brings Commissar Tan here?

161
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:20,000
Chief Guo signed it.

162
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,519
Hurry up and arrange the specific time.

163
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,480
Dr. Chen, I'm heading out.

164
00:10:25,919 --> 00:10:26,519
Take care.

165
00:10:27,399 --> 00:10:28,759
Message me on WeChat, okay, Dr. Chen?

166
00:10:28,879 --> 00:10:29,320
Okay, okay.

167
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,519
Why are you running off so fast?

168
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:36,960
What else should I do?

169
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,480
Wait around for your ideological lecture?

170
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,320
What lecture?

171
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,600
It's already noon, time to eat.

172
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,600
The Courtyard, let's go.

173
00:10:41,799 --> 00:10:42,840
I still have things to do at the station.

174
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:45,879
Aren't you interested in the Dai Mingming case?

175
00:10:52,159 --> 00:10:52,840
Old Wei.

176
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,159
Which room is it?

177
00:10:55,399 --> 00:10:57,080
Keep walking in. Keep going, keep going.

178
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:57,519
Brother Tan.

179
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,080
Which room did you book?

180
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,200
The one on the right.

181
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:04,600
Let's order.

182
00:11:05,159 --> 00:11:05,759
Okay.

183
00:11:16,519 --> 00:11:17,279
Chief Ji

184
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,360
Haven't seen you here in a while.

185
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,679
I've been quite busy lately.

186
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:23,240
Here, bro, take a look.

187
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,399
Any new dishes?

188
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:25,879
Spicy crab.

189
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:26,639
Sounds good.

190
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:27,200
We'll take one.

191
00:11:27,279 --> 00:11:27,879
Coming right up.

192
00:11:28,919 --> 00:11:29,879
Garlic water spinach.

193
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,080
Spicy boiled meat.

194
00:11:32,279 --> 00:11:32,679
Alright.

195
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:33,240
Make it beef.

196
00:11:34,679 --> 00:11:35,399
What would you like for a staple?

197
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:38,679
Anything is fine.

198
00:11:39,639 --> 00:11:40,480
The scallion pancakes are good.

199
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:41,720
We'll take an order.

200
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:42,799
Sure, two pieces.

201
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:43,879
Two pieces, coming right up.

202
00:11:44,559 --> 00:11:45,200
Alright, that's it.

203
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,200
I'll brew you a pot of good tea.

204
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,480
What's going on with Dai Mingming?

205
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,559
Tell me. What's going on with you?

206
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:03,720
What happened? Why did you end up at Chen Meihua's?

207
00:12:04,759 --> 00:12:06,159
Tell me, let me analyze it for you.

208
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:10,080
An article I wrote in college won an award.

209
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,000
Do you remember?

210
00:12:11,279 --> 00:12:12,240
It was called...

211
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:16,279
How to Help Grassroots Police

212
00:12:16,879 --> 00:12:18,200
Relieve Work Stress.

213
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,559
Right, that article won an award.

214
00:12:22,279 --> 00:12:23,600
Tell me, let me analyze it for you.

215
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:26,120
Eat. Let's eat first. Let's eat.

216
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:27,960
After we eat,

217
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,159
I'll tell you what's going on with Dai Mingming.

218
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:49,320
Mingming!

219
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:53,000
Chief Ji, you... please go back inside.

220
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,600
I'll teach him. I'll teach him.

221
00:12:54,759 --> 00:12:55,559
Don't get your hands dirty.

222
00:12:55,639 --> 00:12:56,480
Go inside and have some tea.

223
00:12:56,799 --> 00:12:59,000
Come, come. Come inside and sit.

224
00:12:59,879 --> 00:13:00,200
Here.

225
00:13:03,399 --> 00:13:05,840
Have some tea first. Have a seat.

226
00:13:07,039 --> 00:13:08,639
Mingming, Mom will teach you.

227
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:09,799
Use this.

228
00:13:10,679 --> 00:13:11,639
Don't pick it up! Don't pick it up!

229
00:13:12,039 --> 00:13:12,679
With Mingming here,

230
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,159
he's caused you trouble again.

231
00:13:14,159 --> 00:13:15,120
It's fine, it's fine.

232
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:15,960
You didn't cut your hand, right?

233
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,360
Nobody move. Leave it for now.

234
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:18,759
Uh, let me... let me handle it.

235
00:13:18,799 --> 00:13:19,919
You go ahead. I'll teach him. I'll teach him.

236
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,399
Okay, okay.

237
00:13:20,399 --> 00:13:21,480
Mingming, don't touch it anymore.

238
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,960
Don't touch it. Don't touch it.

239
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:23,679
You arranged this?

240
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,120
Don't cut your hands. Don't cut your hands.

241
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,399
I discussed it with Old Wei.

242
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,399
To let the mother and son work here temporarily,

243
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,399
so their daily meals are covered.

244
00:13:39,759 --> 00:13:40,720
Peanuts and edamame.

245
00:13:43,519 --> 00:13:44,000
Old Wei.

246
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:46,559
Sorry for the trouble.

247
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:48,399
What are you talking about?

248
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,320
It's no trouble at all.

249
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:52,039
If you guys hadn't helped me out back then,

250
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,600
I'd still be messing around on the streets.

251
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,320
Who knows if I'd even be alive right now.

252
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,399
This is nothing.

253
00:13:57,039 --> 00:13:59,440
Well, then... please bear with them.

254
00:13:59,799 --> 00:14:01,679
If you have any difficulties in the future, just tell me.

255
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,799
Chief Ji, really, there's no need to be so polite.

256
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,320
It's just adding two extra pairs of chopsticks.

257
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,000
I'll go check on the food.

258
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:19,600
Chief Ji,

259
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:21,440
thank you so much

260
00:14:21,799 --> 00:14:23,440
for arranging work for Mingming here.

261
00:14:23,639 --> 00:14:25,000
Now that he can support himself,

262
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,600
I can finally feel at ease.

263
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:30,720
Old Wei is a good man.

264
00:14:31,039 --> 00:14:32,200
Leaving your child here,

265
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:33,080
you can rest assured.

266
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:34,720
I know.

267
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,799
The two of us are just a burden here.

268
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,080
Water spinach.

269
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,000
Thank you.

270
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,440
Your happiness is what matters most in our family.

271
00:15:18,559 --> 00:15:20,639
Tell me, what's going on with you?

272
00:15:20,799 --> 00:15:22,559
You even went looking for Chen Meihua.

273
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,120
Commissar Tan.

274
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:39,360
You don't have to stay in the unit every day,

275
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,600
especially at night.

276
00:15:41,279 --> 00:15:42,759
Go home when you should.

277
00:15:44,759 --> 00:15:47,919
Didn't we agree to eat and live together?

278
00:15:48,399 --> 00:15:49,759
We can't give up halfway.

279
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,200
No one's asking you to give up halfway.

280
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,559
I'm just worried it'll affect your family.

281
00:15:58,919 --> 00:16:00,120
My wife already said,

282
00:16:00,159 --> 00:16:01,159
if I don't achieve something,

283
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,519
I shouldn't even think about coming home.

284
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:05,360
You set the bar so high.

285
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:08,039
I have a family, a wife, and kids.

286
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,639
Should I go home at night or not?

287
00:16:09,679 --> 00:16:10,159
Tell me.

288
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:12,519
Captain Liu, you just go home.

289
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,120
We have different responsibilities.

290
00:16:15,639 --> 00:16:16,799
You said it, Commissar.

291
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,320
I did.

292
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,000
Good.

293
00:16:21,159 --> 00:16:21,679
Captain Liao.

294
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:31,120
Captain Liao.

295
00:16:31,919 --> 00:16:35,080
Today, I formally brought up to Chief Guo

296
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,279
the matter of our SWAT detachment

297
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,559
needing a competition venue.

298
00:16:39,639 --> 00:16:40,320
Is it resolved?

299
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,759
Not for now.

300
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:43,919
But

301
00:16:44,559 --> 00:16:47,080
I got us an opportunity to visit

302
00:16:47,759 --> 00:16:48,840
the general headquarters.

303
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,600
What's there to see at the general headquarters?

304
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,759
For this year's skills competition,

305
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,039
they're using the international format.

306
00:16:57,559 --> 00:17:00,200
The general headquarters built a new venue.

307
00:17:01,679 --> 00:17:03,759
It's the venue for the competition.

308
00:17:05,319 --> 00:17:06,200
That's great news.

309
00:17:07,559 --> 00:17:09,440
We can check out the venue in advance,

310
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:09,759
right?

311
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,920
And we can do targeted training.

312
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:12,359
Great news.

313
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:12,680
Yes.

314
00:17:13,359 --> 00:17:14,559
Let's find time to go together.

315
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,039
One more thing.

316
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,039
I've made an appointment with Dr. Chen.

317
00:17:19,039 --> 00:17:20,000
Tomorrow at 1:00 PM.

318
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:23,200
I must thank you for this, Commissar Tan.

319
00:17:23,519 --> 00:17:24,920
You definitely have to thank me.

320
00:17:25,359 --> 00:17:26,240
They have a rule.

321
00:17:26,559 --> 00:17:28,960
Visitors must be escorted by an officer.

322
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:29,599
You go.

323
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:32,759
I'm leading target practice tomorrow.

324
00:17:33,359 --> 00:17:33,960
How about this.

325
00:17:34,519 --> 00:17:36,920
You accompany Naonao to the doctor tomorrow.

326
00:17:37,519 --> 00:17:38,640
I'll lead the target practice.

327
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,559
It's been a long time.

328
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:42,559
I haven't even been to our smart shooting range yet.

329
00:17:43,359 --> 00:17:44,279
Smart shooting range?

330
00:17:45,559 --> 00:17:46,519
I haven't been there either.

331
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,480
I've never been.

332
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,319
Then let's swap tomorrow.

333
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:56,960
Alright, alright.

334
00:17:58,680 --> 00:17:59,599
It's a deal.

335
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:05,640
Good night.

336
00:18:07,799 --> 00:18:08,279
Done washing up.

337
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:09,319
Done washing up.

338
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:10,359
Done washing up.

339
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:11,440
Good night. Good night.

340
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,400
Why did you ask him to do that?

341
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,640
He'll just get in the way.

342
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,319
Just putting some pressure on him.

343
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:41,240
What has your Chief Ji been busy with today?

344
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:47,599
Chief Ji came back from the municipal bureau this afternoon,

345
00:18:48,039 --> 00:18:48,920
and received a call.

346
00:18:49,839 --> 00:18:51,720
A tenant complained about upstairs noise.

347
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,279
Chief Ji went over to mediate the dispute.

348
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:56,480
Around evening,

349
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,319
there was a car accident at East Bridge.

350
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,839
She took a team there for backup.

351
00:19:00,559 --> 00:19:01,680
Tonight, she went out on another call.

352
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,559
The downstairs tenant wasn't satisfied.

353
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,119
He went up and smashed their door.

354
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,240
The upstairs neighbors called the police again.

355
00:19:11,119 --> 00:19:12,319
For all these things, does Chief Ji

356
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:14,640
have to handle them all?

357
00:19:16,799 --> 00:19:17,680
Wherever there's an incident,

358
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,359
that's where you'll find Chief Ji.

359
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:23,359
I've never seen a leader as busy as her.

360
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:25,880
Commissar Tan,

361
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,839
you should know this better than I do.

362
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:38,359
How do you think your Chief Ji handles

363
00:19:39,839 --> 00:19:40,519
all these tasks?

364
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,039
We're just chatting.

365
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:49,359
I also want to know what she's like at work.

366
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:01,839
She's very serious.

367
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,279
And very rational.

368
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,079
It seems like nothing

369
00:20:08,519 --> 00:20:10,359
can ever affect her emotions.

370
00:20:13,559 --> 00:20:14,119
Commissar Tan,

371
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,400
is Chief Ji like this in her personal life too?

372
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:26,599
Commissar Tan,

373
00:20:27,279 --> 00:20:28,519
when you guys were in college,

374
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:29,680
what was Chief Ji like?

375
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:35,480
In college?

376
00:20:39,359 --> 00:20:40,400
Just as busy.

377
00:20:41,559 --> 00:20:42,880
Like a little sun.

378
00:20:44,759 --> 00:20:48,880
Bringing warmth and sunshine to others.

379
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,920
Chief Ji had a side like that?

380
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:53,279
She did.

381
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:56,759
Well, I remember when we were sophomores.

382
00:20:57,359 --> 00:20:58,200
In our second year of college.

383
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:00,839
The school held a singing competition once.

384
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:05,400
My teachers and classmates all urged me to join.

385
00:21:05,759 --> 00:21:07,039
Because I sang well!

386
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:08,640
Really.

387
00:21:09,079 --> 00:21:10,759
Especially the song "Yi Jian Mei."

388
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:14,279
But whenever I got on stage,

389
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,359
my legs would start shaking.

390
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,880
And my palms would sweat.

391
00:21:18,359 --> 00:21:19,000
My pitch...

392
00:21:19,799 --> 00:21:20,880
would go who knows where.

393
00:21:23,839 --> 00:21:24,880
I couldn't go and embarrass myself.

394
00:21:25,799 --> 00:21:26,839
Embarrassing myself was out of the question.

395
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,680
Chief Ji found out and came looking for me.

396
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:33,319
Tan Yan,

397
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:37,000
you should stand on that stage and sing!

398
00:21:37,319 --> 00:21:38,640
Sing for everyone to hear!

399
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,160
You sing so beautifully.

400
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,440
Chief Ji cared about you that much back then?

401
00:21:45,039 --> 00:21:46,240
Well, wasn't she a little sun?

402
00:21:47,759 --> 00:21:50,359
She'd get close to whoever needed sunshine.

403
00:21:51,799 --> 00:21:53,000
So, I was encouraged by her.

404
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,319
With that encouragement, I went up and sang.

405
00:21:57,079 --> 00:21:58,920
After I got off stage, she rushed in.

406
00:21:59,559 --> 00:22:00,519
Rushed right up to me and said,

407
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:04,319
Tan Yan, Tan Yan, you sang so beautifully!

408
00:22:04,319 --> 00:22:06,519
Really, really, really beautifully!

409
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,680
Her tone of voice back then...

410
00:22:16,519 --> 00:22:17,319
And the look in her eyes...

411
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:23,359
I still remember them to this day.

412
00:22:25,599 --> 00:22:28,319
Is that when you fell for Chief Ji?

413
00:22:34,039 --> 00:22:35,279
At that moment, I thought,

414
00:22:35,359 --> 00:22:37,480
I need to hold on tightly to this little sun.

415
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,079
So how did you manage to hold onto Chief Ji?

416
00:22:42,359 --> 00:22:44,839
That was definitely thanks to my many good qualities.

417
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:47,920
Which good qualities?

418
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:03,279
Go to sleep.

419
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:04,519
Yes.

420
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,400
Good night, Commissar Tan.

421
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:19,480
Good night.

422
00:24:28,039 --> 00:24:29,079
First time here, Commissar Tan.

423
00:24:32,039 --> 00:24:32,519
Commissar.

424
00:24:33,799 --> 00:24:34,480
Captain Liao isn't here.

425
00:24:35,039 --> 00:24:35,720
As is customary,

426
00:24:36,559 --> 00:24:37,680
today you'll have to

427
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,200
personally deploy and command us.

428
00:24:41,519 --> 00:24:42,319
Assemble first.

429
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:43,200
Yes, sir.

430
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:57,559
Comrade Commissar.

431
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:59,559
Assembly complete. Awaiting instructions.

432
00:25:02,279 --> 00:25:04,000
Proceed with the shooting training procedure.

433
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:04,559
Yes, sir.

434
00:25:06,319 --> 00:25:08,359
Team One, set up the observation tent.

435
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:09,759
Team Two, inspect weapons.

436
00:25:10,359 --> 00:25:11,920
Team Three, set up the targets.

437
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:13,079
Move!

438
00:25:24,799 --> 00:25:25,559
How does it feel?

439
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:33,160
Captain Liu.

440
00:25:34,079 --> 00:25:35,119
The "smart" you mentioned

441
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,279
is actually manual.

442
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:40,480
Yeah, manual intelligence, right?

443
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:42,559
For so many years,

444
00:25:42,559 --> 00:25:43,680
we've always trained here.

445
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:44,720
Never changed locations.

446
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:47,279
Commissar Tan,

447
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:51,799
is our smart shooting range only going to

448
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,279
live on paper?

449
00:25:53,440 --> 00:25:54,279
It's been years.

450
00:25:56,359 --> 00:25:57,039
Bai Jiani,

451
00:25:57,680 --> 00:26:00,400
does this range help snipers in any way?

452
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:01,559
Commissar,

453
00:26:01,599 --> 00:26:03,440
my mission is, in any environment,

454
00:26:03,519 --> 00:26:04,480
to hit the target accurately.

455
00:26:05,519 --> 00:26:06,039
Commissar Tan,

456
00:26:06,759 --> 00:26:08,440
our training directions are different.

457
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:09,799
We each have our own goals.

458
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,160
What kind of range do you need?

459
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:14,279
A smart shooting range.

460
00:26:14,839 --> 00:26:16,440
One that simulates all weather conditions,

461
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:18,240
and has various information interference.

462
00:26:19,759 --> 00:26:21,480
Well, this range has all of that.

463
00:26:22,279 --> 00:26:23,240
Wild bees for company,

464
00:26:23,759 --> 00:26:24,880
sparrows as examiners.

465
00:26:27,359 --> 00:26:28,759
Let me check today's forecast.

466
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,640
Today's high is 19 degrees.

467
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,039
Level four east wind.

468
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:36,480
Level three UV index.

469
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:38,000
Humidity at 43 percent,

470
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,400
visibility at 28 kilometers.

471
00:26:40,279 --> 00:26:41,480
Throw in some snow,

472
00:26:42,079 --> 00:26:42,920
hail,

473
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,119
or rain,

474
00:26:45,039 --> 00:26:46,559
and it's more real than a smart range.

475
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:55,079
Commissar Tan,

476
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,519
the thing is, this smart range...

477
00:26:58,519 --> 00:26:59,240
The higher-ups

478
00:26:59,799 --> 00:27:00,759
promised it to us long ago.

479
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:04,480
There isn't one in all of Hongye City.

480
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:07,200
Then they shouldn't make empty promises.

481
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,839
We must have ideals,

482
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,599
but these temporary difficulties,

483
00:27:13,359 --> 00:27:14,720
we have to adapt to them.

484
00:27:16,359 --> 00:27:17,279
Adapt to local conditions.

485
00:27:17,599 --> 00:27:18,480
Make do with what we have.

486
00:27:21,799 --> 00:27:22,319
The wind's picking up.

487
00:27:24,279 --> 00:27:26,000
Move! The wind's picking up!

488
00:27:28,119 --> 00:27:28,839
Move!

489
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:29,880
The wind's picking up! The wind's picking up!

490
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:32,960
Take your positions!

491
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:35,160
Ready!

492
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:55,440
About face.

493
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:56,880
Forward, march.

494
00:27:59,519 --> 00:28:00,240
Next group, get ready.

495
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:31,559
Commissar

496
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:32,920
Binoculars

497
00:28:33,079 --> 00:28:33,759
Record this for me.

498
00:29:22,759 --> 00:29:23,400
Naonao.

499
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:26,680
You're amazing. You won again.

500
00:29:29,359 --> 00:29:30,359
Here's your prize.

501
00:29:30,839 --> 00:29:32,680
Look, you already have so many prizes.

502
00:29:39,559 --> 00:29:40,839
But Auntie isn't ready to give up.

503
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:43,680
Auntie wants to play with you again. Okay?

504
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:47,319
Let's have one more match then.

505
00:29:47,759 --> 00:29:48,799
First one to finish building wins.

506
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:54,839
You don't need to worry.

507
00:29:55,319 --> 00:29:56,440
Dr. Chen is very experienced.

508
00:29:58,519 --> 00:29:59,039
Have some tea.

509
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:17,039
I still remember the first time Naonao got sick.

510
00:30:17,039 --> 00:30:18,119
We rushed him to the hospital.

511
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:21,960
While waiting for the results,

512
00:30:24,039 --> 00:30:25,440
I was so nervous my stomach cramped.

513
00:30:27,759 --> 00:30:29,119
Later, the doctor said he was fine.

514
00:30:30,920 --> 00:30:32,599
I just turned and threw up in the toilet.

515
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:35,160
I threw up so much I almost puked bile.

516
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,119
All parents are like that.

517
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:42,880
My mom was the same.

518
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:47,440
When I was a kid,

519
00:30:48,799 --> 00:30:49,640
I was frail and sickly,

520
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:50,839
but still a troublemaker.

521
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:54,039
And our family wasn't well-off, either.

522
00:30:55,519 --> 00:30:56,400
Whenever I had a fever,

523
00:30:57,240 --> 00:30:58,160
my mom would get anxious.

524
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,440
She'd wrap me in a blanket

525
00:31:00,559 --> 00:31:01,839
and carry me to the town hospital.

526
00:31:02,359 --> 00:31:03,279
That was several kilometers away.

527
00:31:05,799 --> 00:31:07,319
Only when my fever finally broke

528
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:09,440
could my mom get some sleep.

529
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:17,240
Parents are the same everywhere.

530
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:19,759
No matter how hard or tiring it is,

531
00:31:20,519 --> 00:31:21,799
they just want their kids to live well.

532
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,799
What about Naonao's dad?

533
00:31:27,279 --> 00:31:28,680
I've never seen him come to visit.

534
00:31:43,759 --> 00:31:44,599
Being a father

535
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:46,359
is not just a title,

536
00:31:47,279 --> 00:31:48,079
but also a responsibility.

537
00:31:49,319 --> 00:31:51,759
Not everyone is fit to be a dad.

538
00:31:55,119 --> 00:31:56,319
It must be tough for you,

539
00:31:56,319 --> 00:31:57,480
raising Naonao on your own.

540
00:31:59,599 --> 00:32:01,559
Anyway, if you ever need anything, just let me know.

541
00:32:05,240 --> 00:32:06,440
Thank you, Captain Liao.

542
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:07,160
Don't mention it.

543
00:32:08,359 --> 00:32:09,839
Naonao and I really get along.

544
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:18,680
Mom, I won!

545
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:47,160
4.53 seconds, six out of eight.

546
00:32:49,559 --> 00:32:50,119
Captain Liu.

547
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,720
This score must rank high in Hongye, right?

548
00:32:54,079 --> 00:32:54,960
Not even close.

549
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:56,920
Too slow. Didn't even break four seconds.

550
00:32:57,079 --> 00:32:58,400
It wouldn't even rank in the SWAT team.

551
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:00,279
How embarrassing.

552
00:33:01,359 --> 00:33:02,680
Rapid pistol shooting...

553
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:05,039
Breaking four seconds is a major hurdle.

554
00:33:05,279 --> 00:33:06,279
When I was in the police academy,

555
00:33:06,279 --> 00:33:09,200
my best record was only 3.8 seconds.

556
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:14,640
Commissar Tan, 3.8 seconds isn't slow at all!

557
00:33:15,359 --> 00:33:16,400
You're a pro.

558
00:33:17,119 --> 00:33:18,480
I just have quick hands.

559
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:21,240
Quick hands are a talent too! Are you kidding?

560
00:33:21,559 --> 00:33:23,359
Come on, show us what you've got.

561
00:33:23,839 --> 00:33:24,759
No, no, no.

562
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:29,119
Show us! Show us! Show us!

563
00:33:31,119 --> 00:33:33,319
Come on, Commissar Tan, don't be shy.

564
00:33:34,920 --> 00:33:35,440
Use my gun.

565
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:37,920
Come on, come on, come on!

566
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:38,839
Don't be shy! Don't be shy!

567
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:40,039
Show us what you've got.

568
00:33:42,119 --> 00:33:43,079
Recently,

569
00:33:44,359 --> 00:33:48,119
I heard about a new shooting training method.

570
00:33:50,079 --> 00:33:51,440
Have you heard of distraction training?

571
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:52,160
Yes, I have.

572
00:33:52,559 --> 00:33:54,079
Nowadays, many foreign SWAT teams

573
00:33:54,079 --> 00:33:54,680
train this way.

574
00:33:54,920 --> 00:33:56,640
It significantly improves shooting accuracy.

575
00:33:57,400 --> 00:33:59,519
Right. Basically, while shooting,

576
00:33:59,519 --> 00:34:02,000
you introduce various distractions

577
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:05,359
to simulate real combat unpredictability.

578
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:08,199
Let's give it a try.

579
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:09,840
Let's try it.

580
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:10,320
[Applause]

581
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:14,639
Lu Xiao, you're in charge of distracting him.

582
00:34:17,159 --> 00:34:18,199
Can I distract him however I want?

583
00:34:18,519 --> 00:34:19,760
Just don't touch me.

584
00:34:20,199 --> 00:34:22,400
Then, when do I...

585
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:25,119
The distraction isn't controlled by me.

586
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:26,239
It's up to you.

587
00:34:30,880 --> 00:34:33,000
Commissar Tan is so weak!

588
00:34:33,559 --> 00:34:35,440
Holding a gun makes him freak!

589
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:37,800
Commissar Tan is so weak!

590
00:34:38,199 --> 00:34:40,400
When he pukes, I laugh all week!

591
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:42,559
Commissar Tan is great, so bright!

592
00:34:42,840 --> 00:34:44,480
But he can't sleep at all at night!

593
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:46,679
But he can't sleep at all at night!

594
00:34:53,559 --> 00:34:55,840
3.93 seconds, zero out of eight.

595
00:35:02,199 --> 00:35:04,119
See? The distraction worked.

596
00:35:06,320 --> 00:35:08,320
That's the whole point of distraction training.

597
00:35:08,559 --> 00:35:09,079
That was fast.

598
00:35:09,559 --> 00:35:10,440
Effective experience

599
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:12,280
always comes from profound lessons.

600
00:35:13,039 --> 00:35:14,400
What's the next drill?

601
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:16,400
The next drill...

602
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:18,599
According to the schedule, we're done for today.

603
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:21,400
Captain Liu, what about that drill for what's-his-name?

604
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:24,239
Right, I forgot.

605
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:25,840
Zhang Yongfu, step forward!

606
00:35:26,280 --> 00:35:26,599
Sir!

607
00:35:27,599 --> 00:35:28,599
Prepare for confidence shooting.

608
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:29,159
Yes, sir.

609
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,119
What drill is this?

610
00:35:33,079 --> 00:35:34,800
It's an old tradition in our SWAT team.

611
00:35:35,679 --> 00:35:37,280
Every new comrade who joins the team

612
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:40,360
must go through this on their first visit.

613
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:47,159
What... what is he putting down there?

614
00:35:50,960 --> 00:35:51,559
His phone.

615
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:53,440
The most valuable thing on him.

616
00:36:01,679 --> 00:36:02,480
Not bad.

617
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,880
Although Yongfu is a rookie,

618
00:36:05,599 --> 00:36:08,000
he's very confident in his marksmanship.

619
00:36:08,079 --> 00:36:08,440
[Applause]

620
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:15,239
This is a good tradition.

621
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:17,599
What if he shoots his own stuff?

622
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:21,239
That's actually never happened before.

623
00:36:24,079 --> 00:36:25,280
Actually, no matter how he shoots,

624
00:36:25,920 --> 00:36:27,039
everyone will accept him.

625
00:36:27,599 --> 00:36:28,599
It's just a ritual.

626
00:36:29,480 --> 00:36:29,960
Captain Liu,

627
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:32,239
Commissar Tan technically just joined the team too.

628
00:36:36,280 --> 00:36:37,760
You can just skip this part.

629
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:39,920
I can't skip it.

630
00:36:40,039 --> 00:36:41,840
I really did just join the team.

631
00:36:43,679 --> 00:36:45,000
Then what do you have on you that's valuable?

632
00:36:45,320 --> 00:36:45,760
My phone.

633
00:36:46,639 --> 00:36:48,119
Commissar Tan's phone is the latest model.

634
00:36:48,280 --> 00:36:49,000
I've seen it.

635
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:54,400
The most expensive thing on me isn't actually my phone.

636
00:36:55,719 --> 00:36:56,480
It's my watch.

637
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:58,599
Let me see.

638
00:37:01,239 --> 00:37:01,679
This will do.

639
00:37:02,639 --> 00:37:03,280
It's more expensive than a phone.

640
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:07,599
Hurry.

641
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:16,079
No... no objections, right?

642
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:17,119
No objections.

643
00:37:17,679 --> 00:37:18,480
It's tradition.

644
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:20,280
Lend me your gun.

645
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:24,199
Go ahead.

646
00:37:38,559 --> 00:37:39,119
Commissar Tan.

647
00:37:40,519 --> 00:37:40,840
Good luck.

648
00:38:22,599 --> 00:38:23,320
Commissar Tan

649
00:38:25,079 --> 00:38:26,119
We're shooting the apple,

650
00:38:27,480 --> 00:38:28,519
not the watch!

651
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:31,519
What should we do?

652
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:33,599
I know.

653
00:38:34,559 --> 00:38:36,000
I guess I don't have the nerves for this.

654
00:38:39,440 --> 00:38:39,679
This...

655
00:38:40,079 --> 00:38:41,039
This isn't appropriate.

656
00:38:41,039 --> 00:38:42,039
How... how much did this cost?

657
00:38:42,039 --> 00:38:42,800
You shouldn't have.

658
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:46,480
Don't worry about the money.

659
00:38:48,679 --> 00:38:50,320
I have to respect tradition, after all.

660
00:38:52,599 --> 00:38:54,199
Once I get through this step,

661
00:38:54,199 --> 00:38:56,280
does it mean I'm officially part of the team?

662
00:38:57,280 --> 00:38:57,639
It counts.

663
00:38:59,039 --> 00:38:59,559
It counts.

664
00:38:59,960 --> 00:39:00,679
It counts.

665
00:39:00,719 --> 00:39:01,199
It counts.

666
00:39:52,760 --> 00:39:53,320
I can't.

667
00:39:53,679 --> 00:39:56,039
I can't be a dad. Seriously.

668
00:39:57,880 --> 00:39:59,280
We're not asking you to be his dad.

669
00:40:00,119 --> 00:40:02,000
Just to play the role of his dad.

670
00:40:03,199 --> 00:40:04,239
I'm afraid I won't do a good job.

671
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:05,360
I have no experience with this.

672
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:07,280
Having experience isn't important.

673
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:10,480
What matters is that Naonao trusts you.

674
00:40:11,519 --> 00:40:13,039
His current psychological issues

675
00:40:13,159 --> 00:40:15,639
mainly stem from a lack of security.

676
00:40:16,119 --> 00:40:18,079
Deep down, the role of a father

677
00:40:18,079 --> 00:40:18,960
is missing from his life.

678
00:40:20,119 --> 00:40:22,119
So the best solution

679
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:23,760
is to take the missing part of his life

680
00:40:24,159 --> 00:40:24,840
and fill that void for him.

681
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:27,960
It's fine, Captain Liao. No pressure.

682
00:40:28,840 --> 00:40:30,280
We'll think of another way.

683
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:32,320
It's not about being pressured.

684
00:40:32,840 --> 00:40:34,239
I'm just really afraid I'll mess it up.

685
00:40:34,480 --> 00:40:35,239
Because ever since I was little,

686
00:40:35,239 --> 00:40:36,480
I barely saw my own dad.

687
00:40:37,199 --> 00:40:38,559
You don't have to force the act.

688
00:40:39,039 --> 00:40:39,679
To put it simply,

689
00:40:39,960 --> 00:40:41,320
you just take on the role of a father

690
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:42,079
and fill that void for him.

691
00:40:42,519 --> 00:40:43,559
Just talk to him more.

692
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,039
Show him you care.

693
00:40:45,559 --> 00:40:46,679
Just spend more time playing with him.

694
00:40:48,519 --> 00:40:49,000
Alright then.

695
00:40:51,199 --> 00:40:51,800
Playing is fine.

696
00:41:15,840 --> 00:41:16,360
Brother Feng.

697
00:41:17,599 --> 00:41:19,039
Sister-in-law and the kid went back to the convenience store.

698
00:41:19,599 --> 00:41:20,840
The SWAT team brought them back.

699
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:24,920
We're heading out, Sister Yuan. Get some rest.

700
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:25,239
Thank you.

701
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:32,440
You guys head back and get some rest.

702
00:41:32,440 --> 00:41:33,159
Thanks for your hard work today.

703
00:41:33,320 --> 00:41:34,719
It was nothing. We'll head out now.

704
00:41:34,719 --> 00:41:35,519
Okay. Thank you.

705
00:41:35,599 --> 00:41:35,920
Bye.

706
00:42:15,320 --> 00:42:16,079
That's her.

707
00:42:19,159 --> 00:42:21,119
Bro, you're amazing.

708
00:42:21,840 --> 00:42:23,639
How'd you know tailing Lu Haifeng's men

709
00:42:23,639 --> 00:42:24,679
would lead us to this person?

710
00:42:25,119 --> 00:42:25,400
Well...

711
00:42:28,239 --> 00:42:29,079
You want to know?

712
00:42:33,519 --> 00:42:35,119
I... I'm just a fisherman.

713
00:42:35,119 --> 00:42:36,719
Even if you... you told me, I wouldn't get it.

714
00:42:42,599 --> 00:42:45,039
You're a pretty good guy.

715
00:42:47,519 --> 00:42:48,800
You need to stay alive.

716
00:42:50,360 --> 00:42:51,079
Know what I mean?

717
00:42:53,679 --> 00:42:54,559
I... I get that.

718
00:43:12,400 --> 00:43:13,519
Ji Min really is

719
00:43:13,519 --> 00:43:15,039
someone who loves others more than herself.

720
00:43:15,199 --> 00:43:16,960
A classic obsessive-compulsive personality.

721
00:43:17,239 --> 00:43:18,639
I have an obsessive-compulsive personality?

722
00:43:19,840 --> 00:43:20,440
Lao Liu,

723
00:43:21,079 --> 00:43:21,840
you must be transferred.

724
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,559
When my dad's home, he's always with me.

725
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:26,159
It's just that he's rarely home.

726
00:43:27,039 --> 00:43:29,559
Your back strain is getting worse.

727
00:43:30,199 --> 00:43:31,400
Have some "Spring Snow."

728
00:43:32,679 --> 00:43:34,960
You can name your terms.
